Apple today released new firmware for the AirPods Pro 2, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods-pro/">AirPods Pro 3</a>, and the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods/">AirPods 4</a>. The firmware has a version number of 8B39, up from 8B34 on the &zwnj;AirPods Pro 3&zwnj;, 8B28 on the AirPods Pro 2, and 8B21 on the &zwnj;AirPods 4&zwnj;. <br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-825981" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2021/11/AirPods-Pro-Firmware-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2322" height="1306" /><br/>
<br/>
There is no word on what's included in the firmware, but Apple <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/106340">has a support document</a> with limited notes. Most updates are limited to bug fixes and performance improvements. <br/>
<br/>
